tellraw @a {"text": "The Giza pyramids were raised with inclined ramps, wooden sledges, levers and copper", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "tools, by organised crews of paid labourers rather than slaves. Khufu's pyramid used about", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "2.3 million blocks averaging 2.5 tonnes, placed over roughly twenty years.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Limestone was quarried on site with copper chisels and dolerite pounders; fine Tura", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "limestone casing and Aswan granite came by boat on the Nile flood. Blocks were dragged on", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "sledges over wetted sand (halving friction, as the Djehutihotep tomb painting shows),", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "hauled up ramps, and levered into place. Surveying used plumb bobs, set squares and water-", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "levelled trenches, giving the base a level within about 2 cm.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "See it in context: /function ac:egypt/giza", "color": "aqua"}
